---
import { PageHeader, Prose } from "@yamat47/pylon";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { ABOUT } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title={ABOUT.title}
  description="What the wiki is for, and how its pages treat the sources they draw on."
>
  <PageHeader title={ABOUT.title} />
  <Prose>
    <p>
      omaha is a wiki of American football. It holds schemes, techniques and drills from across
      the whole game, written from what coaches publish about their own systems. It is something to
      turn to when stuck: designing what a team runs, planning for a game and adjusting during it,
      and teaching players.
    </p>

    <h2>How it treats sources</h2>
    <p>
      Every page is written in its own words and links the sources it draws on. A page says whose
      view a claim is. Where coaches disagree, each view is given with the coach's name, and the
      views are not averaged into one.
    </p>
    <p>
      No text, figure or video of a source is copied here. A quotation is at most one sentence,
      kept only where the wording itself is the information, in quotation marks and with its source.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
